  "body": "What happens: the heidenhain, tinyg and carvera posts have no canned cycle. They write a bore (`CycleKind::Bore`) as the expanded chain: feed in, dwell, rapid out. The spindle turns during the rapid out.\n\nExpected: a bore follows the G86 shape (RS-274/NGC, NIST IR 6556): feed in, spindle stop at the bottom, rapid out, spindle start again. A rapid out with the spindle on can leave a spiral mark in the bore wall.\n\nEvidence: `crates/post/tests/bore_cycle.rs`, test `expanding_posts_rapid_out_of_the_bored_hole_and_keep_the_dwell`, pins the current chain. Found while working #1445 slice 2 (boring G86).\n\nNote: a change here changes the posted output of every bore on these posts. The verifier and the simulation read the chain, so they must stay correct.\n\nDone means: the expanded bore on these posts stops the spindle at the bottom and starts it again after the retract, or the post refuses a bore by name. A test pins the result.\n\nPart of #1445\n",
